### DevelopFileLines

```csharp
public class DevelopFileLines : DevelopFile
{
    public DevelopFileLines();
    public DevelopFileLines(DevelopFile file, string? content);
    public Dictionary<int, string> Lines { get; set; }
    public override string ToString() => string.Join("\r\n", Lines.OrderBy(x => x.Key).Select(x => x.Value));
}
```

**Line splitting behavior:**
- Splits on `\r\n` (Windows) first
- Falls back to `\n` (Unix)
- Falls back to `\r` (old Mac)
- Preserves empty lines via `StringSplitOptions.None`
- Reconstructs with `\r\n` via `ToString()`

